     Apply/plan/destroy run in infra/ directly, per environment:
       make -C infra plan ENV=dev / make -C infra apply ENV=prd -->

## Branching

Branch from `main` using `<type>/<short-description>`:

- `feature/…`, `fix/…`, `refactor/…`, `docs/…`, `chore/…`

## Commits

Use [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/):

```
<type>: <short imperative summary>

Optional body explaining the why.
```

Types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `test`, `chore`. Keep commits atomic — one logical
change each.

## Tests

Add or update tests with every behavior change. `make test` must pass before you open a PR.

## Pull requests

1. Branch, commit, and push.
2. Open a PR with a clear summary of **what** changed and **why**, plus how to verify it.
3. Ensure CI (lint + tests) is green.
4. Request review; address feedback with follow-up commits.

## Code style

Formatting and linting are enforced via `make lint` / `make format`. Run them before pushing.
